1c:["$","$L25",null,{"entry":{"slug":"tinyderby","kind":"preview","index":"02","title":"A Tiny Derby, a soccer game with the fun of Subuteo","subject":"TinyDerby","oneLiner":"Aim, charge, release. Football reduced to one gesture, then grown into a full game — a roster, fifteen power-ups, a squad to train and a league — and now close to release.","role":"Design, art direction, engineering","period":"Aug 2026 · close to release","platform":"iOS · Android · Unity","brief":{"challenge":"Reduce football to a single gesture, then find out whether it can carry a whole game — a career, a squad and fifteen ways to bend the rules — without losing what made the first flick fun.","approach":"Lock the gesture first, design the screens before building them, let bots play thousands of matches to balance it, and write every decision down as it is taken.","result":"Close to release, on TestFlight at 2.5.8: a roster shaped in the Player Lab, fifteen power-ups, training that changes the physics, and a league of 128 original clubs."},"visuals":{"a":{"background":"#0043E0","padX":14.3,"padY":14.3,"fit":"contain","shots":[{"src":"/work/tinyderby/01-logo-badge.webp","w":1090,"h":1071,"alt":"The TinyDerby logo."}]},"b":{"background":"#000E6B","padX":7.2,"padY":6.1,"gap":3.9,"radius":16,"shots":[{"src":"/work/tinyderby/02-screen-home.webp","w":470,"h":1022,"alt":"The TinyDerby home screen on a sunny matchday."},{"src":"/work/tinyderby/03-screen-match.webp","w":470,"h":1022,"alt":"A TinyDerby match with power-ups ready to play."}]},"wide":{"background":"#050814","shots":[{"src":"/work/tinyderby/04-lineup.webp","w":1600,"h":900,"alt":"A line-up of TinyDerby players, each with their own face and hair."}]},"wide2":{"background":"#C6FF00","shots":[{"src":"/work/tinyderby/05-powerups.webp","w":1600,"h":900,"alt":"All fifteen TinyDerby power-ups, from Cannon to Rewind."}]}},"metrics":[{"value":"128","label":"original clubs in the league","source":"16 countries × 8 clubs"},{"value":"15","label":"power-ups, playable in every mode","source":"each one approved in play"},{"value":"977","label":"automated checks green","source":"799 match + 178 power-up"}],"summary":["Aim, charge, release. TinyDerby is football reduced to one gesture, and then built out into a full game around it: a roster of players you shape in the Player Lab — face, hair, kit, boots — fifteen power-ups, a squad you train, and Road to Glory, a league of 128 original clubs across 16 countries.","Training is not cosmetic. Five skills — attack, keeper, defence, fitness, accuracy — change the physics of every shot in the league, and going up a division takes both a top-two finish and a squad strong enough to hold the spot."],"process":[{"title":"Lock the gesture first","body":"Aim-and-charge was chosen and then defended against several better-sounding alternatives, each recorded with why it lost."},{"title":"Design the screens before building them","body":"Every screen was a board before it was code — the Player Lab, training, the league table, the power-up catalogue — so the game grew as a product rather than out of the prototype."},{"title":"Let bots play it thousands of times","body":"Balance came out of thousands of automated matches instead of out of taste, and every power-up is tested the way a thumb uses it — press, then release — before it ships."},{"title":"Write the decision down when you make it","body":"Dated, with its consequence and what it replaced. That is what makes a fast sprint reviewable instead of a blur."}],"outcome":["On TestFlight at 2.5.8 and close to release, with the roster, the Player Lab, fifteen power-ups, training, the Road to Glory league and a Fans leaderboard running on its own server.","The bug worth keeping from the first week: every match reported 0-0, because the app around the game restarted the round during the goal celebration and wiped the score it had just recorded."],"learned":"A game can be right in the engine and wrong in the app around it. Everything stayed green the whole time the scoreline was a lie."}}]
